  "titles": {
    "_tiers_note": "Goidelic ladder, ascending, with the Akkadian substrate co-titles beneath. Flaith (noble-lord) barony; Criche-tigerna (border-lord) march; Tigerna (lord) county; Toisech (chieftain/leader) duchy; Ri-tuaithe (king of a tuath) principality over a Tuath (petty kingdom); Ruiri (over-king) kingdom; Ard-ri (high king) empire. The conquered cities keep their Akkadian shaknu (governor) and sangu (priest) beneath the Gaelic crown. The brithem (judge) and the fili/ollam (poet-sage) stand outside the ladder, as does the Akkadian scribal shatammu. Rank titles fuse the real Gaelic and Akkadian registers (allowed).",
    "display_policy": "Ruler/domain titles shown in setting-gen, domain lists and vassal trees are ENGLISH (or an approved commonly-known foreign term where set in 'ruler'). The *_native conlang forms are for NPC DIALOGUE ONLY, never for structural/UI displays.",
